-"abstract": "<jats:p>&lt;p&gt;Token design lacks a coherent discipline. Projects assemble mechanisms from 
-precedent, failures are attributed to market conditions rather than predictable design flaws, and no 
-established field integrates the economics, control theory, game theory, and constitutional design that token 
-systems require. We frame the resulting practice as systems engineering: coordinating autonomous agents under 
-uncertainty while distributing ownership to contributors without centralized enforcement. What distinguishes 
-protocols from historical private currency issuance is programmable enforcement of issuance rules and 
-dissolution of the capital-labor boundary when contribution generates ownership.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We 
-develop MeshNet, a fictional but empirically parameterized decentralized wireless protocol that specifies five 
-integrated mechanisms: productive staking, reputation-weighted governance, burn-mint value capture, conviction 
-voting, and PID-controlled adaptive emissions. Parameters are calibrated to Helium hardware economics, 
-Filecoin collateral ratios, and governance data from 12 DePIN protocols. A 240-run agent-based ensemble, 
-supplemented by 566 sensitivity and adversarial runs, stress-tests these mechanisms over five years under four 
-macroeconomic scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Three findings stand out. First, adaptive emission functions as 
-insurance: the PID controller compresses worst-case variance by 6× (coefficient of variation from 0.544 to 
-0.087 under competitor shock) while sustaining 8,880 nodes at the 5th percentile versus 1,049 under static 
-policy. Second, this advantage is conditional: bull markets produce identical outcomes, and the engineering 
-premium emerges only under sustained contraction. Third, without pre-planned guardrails the controller can 
-trigger integral wind-up, reinforcing the case for simulation-first design methodology. Reputation-weighted 
-governance reduces voting-power concentration (Gini from 0.89 to 0.72). The design methodology generalizes to 
-token economies facing analogous coordination problems.&lt;/p&gt;</jats:p>", "author": [ { "affiliation": [], 
